"version9_60onboardingCardDescription" = "Welcome to version 9.60 of MirrorHR Epilepsy Research Kit: even easier to use and full of features.
MirrorHR is a free, safe, and private app developed by parents and doctors for parents and doctors.
Some features, such as real-time heart rate monitoring and alarms, require an Apple Watch (running WatchOS 8+) connected to iPhone (running iOS 15+). However, if you don't have an Apple Watch, the application is still highly beneficial for recording all events and symptoms and promoting better communication with your doctor.
MirrorHR is not a medical device, nor does it intend to be: it just wants to help you learn more about the epilepsy of your loved ones in alliance with your doctor.

Among the significant innovations of this version:
1. Improved Apple Watch control for real-time monitoring management.
2. Improved data export to Excel to facilitate data sharing with your doctor.
3. Possibly pre-populate an email for your doctor with the data of the last epileptic seizure.
4. New symptoms are available in the diary, and it is now possible to enter the precise duration of a symptom or event.
5. Fixed some bugs and performance improvements.

We also remind you that MirrorHR is entirely anonymous, and the data is only on your phone.
Real-time monitoring requires pairing with an Apple Watch.
After the update, we recommend restarting the Apple Watch to ensure that the two applications (on the iPhone and the Apple Watch) are correctly aligned.

A special thanks to two super mothers who have continuously given us suggestions for improving MirrorHR: thank you very much, Stefania and Elena. #NeverStopFighting

If you want to help us make MirrorHR Epilepsy Research Kit even more helpful, please get in touch with us at helpme@mirrorhr.org and post a review on the Apple App Store.

Thank you for contributing to the epilepsy research together.
";

